  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Ayush has two rooted trees. Each of them contains NNN vertices (numbered 111 through NNN); let's denote a vertex vvv in tree 111 by v1v_1v1​ and a corresponding vertex vvv in tree 222 by v2v_2v2​.\n\nFor each tree ttt, any vertex on the path from the root to a vertex vtv_tvt​ (including vtv_tvt​) is an ancestor of vtv_tvt​ and the depth of vtv_tvt​ is the distance of vtv_tvt​ from the root of tree ttt.\n\nFor any integer www (1≤w≤N1 \\le w \\le N1≤w≤N) and vertices u1u_1u1​ and v2v_2v2​, www is said to be a common ancestor of u1u_1u1​ and v2v_2v2​ if:\n\n\nin tree 111, w1w_1w1​ is an ancestor of u1u_1u1​\nin tree 222, w2w_2w2​ is an ancestor of v2v_2v2​\nthe depths of vertices w1w_1w1​ and w2w_2w2​ (from their respective roots) are the same\nFor example, in the figure above, the pair (u1,v2)=(6,1)(u_1, v_2) = (6, 1)(u1​,v2​)=(6,1) has two common ancestors — 444 and 666. Although vertex 222 is an ancestor for each of them, the depths of 212_121​ and 222_222​ are not the same.\n\nHelp Ayush find the maximum number of common ancestors for a pair of vertices, i.e. the largest integer ccc such that there is a pair of vertices (u1,v2)(u_1, v_2)(u1​,v2​) (possibly u=vu = vu=v) with ccc common ancestors.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\le T \\le 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1061 \\le N \\le 10^61≤N≤106",
      "1≤pi,qi≤N1 \\leq p_i, q_i \\leq N1≤pi​,qi​≤N for each valid iii",
      "p1,p2,…,pNp_1, p_2, \\ldots, p_Np1​,p2​,…,pN​ describe a tree with exactly one root",
      "q1,q2,…,qNq_1, q_2, \\ldots, q_Nq1​,q2​,…,qN​ describe a tree with exactly one root",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10610^6106"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers p1,p2,…,pNp_1, p_2, \\ldots, p_Np1​,p2​,…,pN​. For each valid iii, pip_ipi​ is the parent of the vertex i1i_1i1​ or −1-1−1 if the vertex i1i_1i1​ is the root of tree 111.\nThe third line contains NNN space-separated integers q1,q2,…,qNq_1, q_2, \\ldots, q_Nq1​,q2​,…,qN​. Similarly, for each valid iii, qiq_iqi​ is the parent of the vertex i2i_2i2​ or −1-1−1 if the vertex i2i_2i2​ is the root of tree 222.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer — the maximum number of common ancestors for a pair (u1,v2)(u_1, v_2)(u1​,v2​).",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n1\n-1\n-1\n3\n2 -1 2\n2 -1 1\n7\n2 3 -1 2 2 4 4\n6 -1 4 5 2 4 4",
        "output": "1\n2\n2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: There is only one pair (u1,v2)=(11,12)(u_1, v_2) = (1_1, 1_2)(u1​,v2​)=(11​,12​) and only one common ancestor.\nExample case 2: If u=1u = 1u=1, then 111 and 222 are common ancestors for any vvv.\nExample case 3: The maximum number of common ancestors is 222, e.g. 444 and 666 for (u1,v2)=(6,1)(u_1, v_2) = (6, 1)(u1​,v2​)=(6,1), as shown in the figure in the statement."
      }
    ]
  },
